-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Discriminator Reuse:** Reusing a pre-trained discriminator yields inferior results; it must be retrained alongside each new reconstruction to provide feedback for different aspects of the solution [S3].
-*   **Batch & Resolution Handling:** The relativistic GAN 'average' formulation allows different resolutions and batch sizes for real and fake samples, while the least-squares variant gives empirically better results [S3].
-*   **Loss Balancing:** The relative weights ($\lambda$) of the adversarial loss versus reconstruction losses must be carefully tuned to prevent the discriminator from overpowering the generator [S1].
 
